WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.340
Your skin is for feeling.

2
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.580
Even when you cannot see, your hands tell you if something is rough or smooth, hard

3
00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:11.300
or soft, warm or cold.

4
00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:13.680
Touch is one of your five senses.

5
00:00:14.783 --> 00:00:18.563
You need a pillowcase and eight to ten objects with different textures.

6
00:00:19.543 --> 00:00:23.863
Keep a metal spoon, a wooden spoon, and a spoon from the fridge aside for later.

7
00:00:24.917 --> 00:00:26.117
Pack the bag yourself.

8
00:00:27.057 --> 00:00:31.517
Your child feels one object without looking and gives three describing words, then

9
00:00:31.517 --> 00:00:34.817
guesses. Later, add the metal and wooden spoons.

10
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.110
Most children find the metal spoon feels colder, though both are at room

11
00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:44.090
temperature. A cold spoon can feel wet, so check it with a towel.

12
00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:46.190
Touch cannot tell colour.

13
00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:48.030
Only your eyes can.

14
00:00:48.933 --> 00:00:51.393
Stay with your child and check every object.

15
00:00:52.373 --> 00:00:55.353
Use objects too big to fit inside a toilet paper tube.

16
00:00:56.193 --> 00:00:59.993
Nothing sharp, hot, frozen, breakable, or alive goes in the bag.
